  "findings": [
    "Stationary broad and fine terms pay approximately -1.7 reward/s in low and middle standing groups; the broad pseudo-Huber cost remains unbounded. Current failure is not explained by an absent stationary reward or the old 0.03 scale.",
    "State-independent learned action standard deviations grow. Noise remains present at zero visible velocity/yaw commands; stronger shared exploration is a mechanically plausible contributor, not a completed PPO causal ablation.",
    "Wheel near-limit requested torque rises to roughly 27-32% of physics samples in low/middle standing groups; leg near-limit requests remain below 0.7%. This does not support low/middle leg torque saturation by the gas spring as the primary explanation.",
    "quiet_velocity_weight and quiet_wheel_weight belong to the non-SCUT branch. zero_command_velocity_scale multiplies the legacy stand_translation term which apply_dense_tracking removes; it does not multiply dense_stationary terms.",
    "Signed velocity means are small while absolute planar speeds remain large. Opposite environment biases and temporal oscillations cannot be separated by aggregate means alone.",
    "Ordinary passive RECOVERY occupancy rises at low height, but reward_support_tracking override keeps ordinary stationary/height costs active. RECOVERY is not evidence that robots are fallen or executing RMCS self-righting."
  ],
  "pending_causal_validation": "At independent resources or natural domain end, replay one sealed checkpoint with fixed seeds/initial states and unchanged command groups. Pair sampled vs deterministic actions with identical delay, then deterministic full-delay vs clean feedback. Measure body velocity, individual wheel/reference traces, height/attitude and requested/applied torque. Do not hot-change reward, noise, ABI, architecture or running contract from this audit."
